# Pre-PR quality gate (build + static check)

CI builds every PlatformIO environment on every pull request. Catch failures locally **before** the first push and **before** marking a PR ready for review or merge.

## Required command

From the repo root (PlatformIO installed, `pip install platformio` or `uv tool install platformio`):

```bash
scripts/lint-gate.sh
```

It runs `pio run` for every environment in `platformio.ini` and `pio check` (cppcheck) on the firmware sources, the same surface area as the CI **Build** job.

## When to run

- **Before every `git push`** on a feature branch (humans: enable `.githooks` — see below).
- **Before opening or updating a PR**, and again after any commit that touches firmware sources or `platformio.ini`.
- **Cloud agents:** run `scripts/lint-gate.sh` before the first push each turn that includes code changes; do not mark a draft PR **ready for review** until it passes locally and the CI Build check is green.

## Git pre-push hook (local)

One-time setup per clone:

```bash
scripts/setup-git-hooks.sh
```

The pre-push hook runs `scripts/lint-gate.sh` and blocks the push if the build or static check fails.

## Merge policy

Do not merge a PR while the **Build** workflow is failing. Prefer fixing the build on the branch over follow-up fix commits on `main`.

On GitHub, enable branch protection on `main` with the Build workflow as a **required status check** so merges cannot bypass CI (repo admin setting).
